{% comment %}
  Renders Melt's logo as an inline SVG.

  Shopify's image_picker setting won't accept an SVG, so the mark lives in
  assets/melt-logo.svg and is inlined here instead. Being inline means it stays
  crisp at any size, costs no extra request, and fills with currentColor — so
  by default it follows the colour scheme it sits in.

  Wherever a logo can be set (Theme settings → Logo, Theme settings → Brand
  information), a "Logo type" setting picks between this SVG and an uploaded
  image. If "Image" is chosen but nothing is uploaded, callers fall back to this.

  Accepts:
  - class: {String} Optional additional classes for the wrapper.
  - color: {String} 'auto' (follow colour scheme), 'dark' or 'light'. Defaults to 'auto'.
  - width: {Number} Optional width in px. Omit when the caller sizes the wrapper in CSS.

  Usage:
  {% render 'melt-logo', color: settings.logo_svg_color, class: 'header__heading-logo-wrapper' %}
{% endcomment %}

<span
  class="melt-logo-wrapper melt-logo-wrapper--{{ color | default: 'auto' }}{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
  {% if width %}
    style="width: {{ width }}px; max-width: 100%;"
  {% endif %}
>
  {{- 'melt-logo.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
</span>
<span class="visually-hidden">{{ shop.name }}</span>
